{"agent":"lane-sw-3","data":{"budget":"5 min","claim":"No: the lease object keeps the worktree and branch, but no event names a restore condition, so nothing can derive RESUME-READY.","falsifier":"git grep finds a park or restore-condition event kind on main.","item":"DX-park-and-resume","mechanism":"The break, expire and forced-release paths append only lease.expired or lease.released; no event kind or fold carries a restore condition.","probe":"git grep -c \"lane.parked\" main -- ddflow","probe_output":"(no matches, exit 1 from git grep; the shell echo printed 0 for head)","question":"Does a lease that ends with a worktree (break, expiry, forced release) leave any record of why and what restores it on main today?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e9dda2e3f4e299b9044766e7a","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":184965,"schema":1,"subject":"R7cbeaff3f0","ts":"2026-11-12T15:45:46.079839Z"}
